## Goal
Produce a sample-level PCA from the resolved gene count matrix and show whether samples
separate by treatment status, with points coloured treated versus untreated.

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| counts_gene | rnaseq_bulk / 01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |
| design | stage 01 samplesheet output | 01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv |

## Method
1. In the `gars-bio` environment, read the gene count TSV and stage 01 design CSV; match
   columns to `sample_id` values and retain samples present in both inputs.
2. Transform counts with `log2(count + 1)`, center and scale each gene across samples, then
   compute PCA using scikit-learn `PCA(n_components=2, svd_solver="full")`.
3. Save the first two principal component scores and the treatment label for each sample as
   `results/pca_scores.csv`. Plot PC1 versus PC2, colour by `condition` (treated or untreated),
   label points by sample ID, and save as `results/sample_pca.png`.
4. Scripts read inputs without modifying them. Run the analysis as a batch job using the
   configured executor.

## Outputs
Types come from the closed vocabulary in _references/artifact_types.md.

| File | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| results/pca_scores.csv | table | Sample PCA coordinates and treatment labels |
| results/sample_pca.png | figure | PC1 versus PC2, points coloured by treatment status |

